WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.243
Effective threat hunting depends on meaningful telemetry.

2
00:00:03.243 --> 00:00:12.981
Analysts need data that reflects activity across important systems and enough context to distinguish expected operations from behavior that deserves further review.

3
00:00:12.981 --> 00:00:21.572
Endpoint telemetry can describe system activity, software execution, security events, connections, and changes over time.

4
00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:29.314
Its value increases when records include stable asset identifiers, accurate timestamps, ownership, and business context.

5
00:00:29.314 --> 00:00:34.024
Authentication and identity records help hunters understand access patterns.

6
00:00:34.024 --> 00:00:45.598
Sign-in events, privilege changes, account lifecycle information, and identity-provider context can show whether activity aligns with a user's role and normal operating conditions.

7
00:00:45.598 --> 00:00:48.402
Network telemetry provides another perspective.

8
00:00:48.402 --> 00:01:00.624
Connection metadata, name-resolution records, approved security-device logs, and traffic summaries can reveal relationships among systems without relying on a single endpoint data source.

9
00:01:00.624 --> 00:01:03.807
Cloud and application logs are increasingly important.

10
00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:15.571
Control-plane events, workload records, application audit trails, and service activity can help explain what occurred in environments that traditional network monitoring may not fully represent.

11
00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:19.822
Asset inventories and configuration information supply context.

12
00:01:19.822 --> 00:01:31.954
A record becomes more useful when the hunter knows whether the system is production or development, internet facing or internal, business critical or temporary, and managed by which team.

13
00:01:31.954 --> 00:01:34.798
Data quality determines investigative quality.

14
00:01:34.798 --> 00:01:46.093
Missing time periods, inconsistent clocks, duplicate records, short retention, unclear field definitions, and incomplete coverage can lead to incorrect conclusions.

15
00:01:46.093 --> 00:01:48.877
Hunts should document these limitations explicitly.

16
00:01:48.877 --> 00:01:51.761
Telemetry access also requires governance.

17
00:01:51.761 --> 00:02:02.407
Organizations should apply authorization, privacy, retention, and need-to-know requirements so investigations use security data responsibly and maintain appropriate oversight.
